{"issue": true, "summary": "The `shouldConsumeRetry` option is called with a context that has `retryDelay` set to 0 when retries are exhausted, but it should be set to the actual delay that would have been used if retries were not exhausted.", "edits": [{"path": "index.js", "old": "const consumeRetryContext = Object.freeze({
	error: normalizedError,
	attemptNumber,
	retriesLeft,
	retriesConsumed,
	retryDelay: retriesLeft > 0 ? delayTime : 0,
});", "new": "const consumeRetryContext = Object.freeze({
	error: normalizedError,
	attemptNumber,
	retriesLeft,
	retriesConsumed,
	retryDelay: delayTime,
});"}]}
